49
00:03:09,960 --> 00:03:12,500
And the structure we're building is no exception.

50
00:03:14,320 --> 00:03:26,320
In May of 2002, the Clark Construction Group, the builder and general contractor, broke ground on a $174 million project in downtown Los Angeles.

51
00:03:28,460 --> 00:03:29,291
Their task?

52
00:03:29,292 --> 00:03:37,220
Build a 750,000 square foot office building for the California Department of Transportation, or Caltrans.

53
00:03:37,221 --> 00:03:44,600
The building will take up an entire city block, and although it will rise a relatively modest

54
00:03:44,601 --> 00:03:50,980
13 stories above ground, with four stories of parking below the plaza level, constructing

55
00:03:50,981 --> 00:04:00,900
it will present the same architectural, structural, and mechanical challenges as larger buildings.

56
00:04:00,901 --> 00:04:07,900
construction has 27 months to complete our office building.

57
00:04:08,540 --> 00:04:13,540
Every big building starts with a developer or owner, someone who puts up the money.

58
00:04:13,541 --> 00:04:15,620
The building is the top of you.

59
00:04:15,621 --> 00:04:21,300
Typically the owner selects an architect, someone to design the building.

60
00:04:21,301 --> 00:04:26,660
Sometimes this is done through a design competition, where rivals submit renderings and models of

61
