94
00:07:01,801 --> 00:07:04,980
Others on the team will work on the guts of the building.

95
00:07:04,981 --> 00:07:10,960
If they win the competition, Morphosis will eventually lay out every detail, every column,

96
00:07:10,961 --> 00:07:16,260
window in the form of extremely detailed drawings or construction documents.

97
00:07:19,140 --> 00:07:24,200
The set of documents can be 300 to 400 pages, and they're constantly changing.

98
00:07:25,240 --> 00:07:27,880
Designing is not just making one decision after the other.

99
00:07:28,260 --> 00:07:31,860
It is making a whole bunch of decisions together, and they all have to work together.

100
00:07:32,440 --> 00:07:35,540
Architects don't work in a self-indulgent creative vacuum.

101
00:07:36,020 --> 00:07:39,600
They're governed by planning codes, structural engineering limitations.

102
00:07:40,960 --> 00:07:43,300
The needs of the client.

103
00:07:43,301 --> 00:07:45,560
You can either have moving exhibits,

104
00:07:45,561 --> 00:07:47,560
but you're going to have a very large archive

105
