212
00:14:16,241 --> 00:14:18,240
There's a few different ways to place concrete.

213
00:14:18,241 --> 00:14:21,240
One is you tailgate it out of the back of the truck.

214
00:14:21,241 --> 00:14:26,240
Another way is you pump it into a form or into place

215
00:14:26,241 --> 00:14:28,240
with a concrete pump.

216
00:14:28,241 --> 00:14:30,240
And then there's what is called a shotcrete pump,

217
00:14:30,241 --> 00:14:32,240
which is this application here.

218
00:14:32,241 --> 00:14:38,337
here. Shotcrete is where it's actually blown onto the wall with high air pressure.

219
00:14:38,338 --> 00:14:39,080
It's a lot

220
00:14:39,081 --> 00:14:40,555
faster to install it.

221
00:14:40,556 --> 00:14:45,400
Modern construction couldn't do without the magic concoction of sand,

222
00:14:45,640 --> 00:14:48,088
aggregate, water, and cement.

223
00:14:48,089 --> 00:14:52,900
Although cement mortar dates back to at least the Romans,

224
00:14:53,760 --> 00:14:58,880
modern concrete construction wasn't possible before the invention of Portland cement in 1824

225
00:14:58,881 --> 00:15:01,220
by Joseph Aspden of England.

226
00:15:03,460 --> 00:15:07,120
He burned and ground together a mixture of limestone and clay,

227
00:15:07,900 --> 00:15:09,540
creating modern hydraulic cement.

228
00:15:11,000 --> 00:15:13,980
It hardens with water and gets stronger with time.

229
00:15:15,680 --> 00:15:19,380
By 1900, engineers were using concrete to construct bridges,

230
00:15:19,840 --> 00:15:20,760
streets, and buildings.

231
00:15:23,580 --> 00:15:26,820
To make concrete stronger, builders started embedding

232
00:15:26,821 --> 00:15:28,400
steel reinforcing bar.

233
00:15:28,880 --> 00:15:30,720
or rebar into the concrete.

234
00:15:32,780 --> 00:15:35,060
Concrete performs well under compression,

235
00:15:35,061 --> 00:15:36,720
but not as well under tension.

236
00:15:40,820 --> 00:15:41,920
Steel, on the other hand,

237
00:15:41,921 --> 00:15:43,760
performs much better under tension.

238
00:15:48,400 --> 00:15:52,600
So the two together, the concrete and the reinforcing steel,

239
00:15:52,601 --> 00:15:57,600
will then resist both compression loads and tension loads.

240
00:15:58,880 --> 00:16:05,240
Builders use reinforced concrete in foundations, walls, floors, and sometimes structural columns.

241
00:16:07,440 --> 00:16:12,520
These guys make it look easy, but concrete can be exceptionally tricky once in a while.

242
00:16:12,760 --> 00:16:13,980
Concrete is like a woman.

243
00:16:15,060 --> 00:16:16,520
You have to be patient with it.

244
00:16:16,560 --> 00:16:20,400
It sets up at its own pace, and it's not very agreeable at times.

245
00:16:24,280 --> 00:16:28,100
After the foundation work, it's time to bring in the real men of steel.

